    "answer": {
      "short": "a and e; b and f; c and h; d and g.",
      "worked": "Since $Z$ is continuous, including an endpoint does not change a probability.\n\na and e, by symmetry and the complement rule:\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(Z<-0.6)&=P(Z>0.6)\\\\&=1-P(Z\\le0.6)\\\\&=1-P(Z<0.6)\\\\&\\approx1-0.7257=0.2743.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nb and f, by symmetry: $P(Z\\ge-1.4)=P(Z\\le1.4)\\approx0.9192$.\n\nc and h: $P(Z=3.1)=P(Z=0.5)=0$, since a continuous random variable has zero probability of taking any single value.\n\nd and g: $P(Z\\le2.5)=P(Z<2.5)\\approx0.9938$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
